e who think that maybe to  accede to the demand that ukraine would  never join nato  would be one way of at least getting him  back to the negotiating table  well what it would do is it would give  him something and cause him to think  well what else should i be getting as  well he's not going to stop with getting  his demands met we've seen this this  movie many times  and moreover it is not for us to sign  away the rights of 40 million ukrainians  it is for them to decide the future of  their own country now what the u.s and  europe are doing  is threatening massive retaliatory  sanctions if russia does invade again  increasing these military presence in  nato allies in eastern europe and  increasing security assistance to  ukraine so they can better defend  themselves but all of this is being  framed as a response if russia attacks  again  and i think that what we really should  be doing is taking the all three of  those steps but doing it right away as a  deterrent to such an invasion with a  promise that we could wind down some of  that if russia stands its forces down  and we're no longer negotiating under  the threat of the use of force so you  would stand  next to former secretary of state uh  mike pompeo when he criticizes the biden  administration  for basically talking and not doing um  because uh  pompeo has said that putin is prepared  to  push to the brink is it his expression  in ukraine to get what he wants you are  in favor  of more aggressive tactics  well i wouldn't describe what i said as  aggressive uh i do believe that we need  to be doing rather than talking only  and i think that that he's right about  that but helping a country get the  armaments and training so it can defend  itself is not an aggressive step uh it  is a prudent one to help stave off such  an invasion putting sanctions against a  country that is now using extortionist  type threats against nato against  ukraine against europe um that's not an  unreasonable thing to do either and we'd  be willing to lift those sanctions if  russia stopped its intimidating activity  i don't see these as aggressive moves i  see them as prudent defensive moves to  put in place to try to stave off  something worse  i was interested in the pompeo  intervention is this a sign uh that mr  pompeo is now gearing up for a run in  2024 is this the opening  of the political hostilities  for um the elections  in states later on this year and then  the 2024 uh presidential election yeah i  read an article yesterday  where there was a debate about when did  the 2024 presidential election campaign  begin is it 2022 was it in 2020 just  after the january 6th riots or did it  actually begin in 2020 before the 2020  election and people are already jostling  for 2024. um i think it may have been  the latter as well too  uh  no one knows at this stage who is going  to run on the republican side it is  quite possible that former president  trump would run again there are a number  of strong republican candidates mike  pompeo among them who might want to try  as well  a lot of them are doing the kinds of  things you need to do to prepare so they  can make a decision later if they choose  to run  and i think mike pompeo would be one of  the stronger candidates if he did

